## 12. Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] SDK generation identified and the implementation matches it.
- [ ] An R2 bucket (or prefix) is mounted as a filesystem path in a running sandbox.
- [ ] Data written to the mount is visible in R2 through an independent check.
- [ ] After the sandbox is destroyed, a new sandbox mounting the same key reads the same data without any manual restore step.
- [ ] Data outside the mount is demonstrated not to persist, and this boundary is documented.
- [ ] Standard file operations (shell, Python I/O, SDK file API where available) work on the mounted path.
- [ ] Rename, lock, permission, cache, and interrupted-write differences are handled or documented.
- [ ] The R2 token is scoped to one bucket with Object Read & Write only; secrets are stored only as Worker secrets and never exposed to the sandbox, logs, or source.
- [ ] Read-only mounts are used where the job only reads; prefixes are narrow and isolated.
- [ ] All entry routes are authenticated, and identifiers are validated.
- [ ] Mount errors and busy-unmount cases are handled with sanitized messages.
- [ ] Tests and build were executed, or unverifiable items are explicitly listed with exact commands.
- [ ] No existing feature, bucket, token, or route was changed without authorization.

Do not mark any criterion complete without implementation evidence or an executed test.

